  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 4-Formylaminooxyvinylglycine may interact with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of intermediate targets. The drug appears to target multiple entities, including Lysine-specific demethylase 4A, E-selectin, and gastric inhibitory polypeptide, all of which are known to be targets of other compounds. These targets are ultimately linked to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, indicating a potential pathway where the drug's effects are mediated through these intermediate molecules. The evidence suggests that the drug may influence the activity of Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase indirectly, possibly through the modulation of its downstream targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the drug's potential to modulate metabolic processes by interacting with key enzymes in the glycolytic pathway.",
